# Nomad App - AI Assistant Rules

## Project Context
This is a React Native/Expo trip tracking app called "Nomad" with the following key features:
- GPS location tracking with trip recording
- Map visualization using react-native-maps
- Trip history with export capabilities (GPX/KML)
- Color theming system
- Cross-platform support (iOS, Android, Web)

## Code Standards
- Use TypeScript with strict typing
- Follow React Native best practices
- Implement proper error handling
- Use React.memo, useCallback, useMemo for performance
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use proper naming conventions (camelCase for variables, PascalCase for components)

## Architecture Patterns
- Separate utilities into utils/ directory
- Use custom hooks for complex state logic
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Use context for global state management
- Prefer composition over inheritance

## Performance Guidelines
- Memoize expensive calculations
- Debounce location updates
- Use proper cleanup in useEffect
- Implement loading states for async operations
- Optimize bundle size with tree-shaking

## File Organization
- types/ - TypeScript type definitions
- utils/ - Utility functions
- components/ - Reusable UI components
- hooks/ - Custom React hooks
- app/ - Expo Router pages

## Testing Strategy
- Write unit tests for utility functions
- Test components with React Native Testing Library
- Mock location services for testing
- Test error scenarios

## Deployment
- Use EAS Build for production builds
- Implement proper error reporting
- Monitor performance metrics
- Test on multiple devices and platforms
